        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 0,
        "retweet_count": 11
      },
      "text": "The viral phrase that’s taken over is “data is the new oil”. It’s a little true—data is very valuable, and needs to be refined (labeled).\n\nBut quickly breaks down—data is not a commodity, it’s reusable, and it’s illiquid.\n\nData is far more similar to code.\n\nData is the new code.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1199058252656345089"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2019-11-24T15:56:35.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1198631509139214336"
      ],
      "id": "1198631509139214336",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 3,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 66,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 10
      },
      "text": "One origin of the standup meeting👭\n\nFujio Mitarai, CEO of Canon, noticed that the exec status meetings lasted 2 full days.\n\nIn response, he removed all chairs from the room and forced everyone to stand.\n\nThe meeting became 2 hrs.\n\nHe then wrote a hit book which popularized it.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1198631509139214336"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2019-11-23T19:28:40.000Z",
