      ],
      "text": "Scaling = no capacity constraints\nCompounds = exponential upside\n\nCompounding is a statement on the top-line, and scaling is a statement on the bottom line.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1193772631020822529"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2019-11-10T23:49:31.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1193677093055295488"
      ],
      "id": "1193677093055295488",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 360,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 1588,
        "quote_count": 14,
        "reply_count": 13,
        "retweet_count": 246
      },
      "text": "Simple rule for founders: Only spend your time on things whose value compounds exponentially.\n\nThey don't need to scale, but they need to compound.\n\nExamples:\n- Hiring\n- Culture\n- Code\n- Understanding of customer\n- Internal memos\n- Relationships\n- Internal alignment",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1193677093055295488"
    },
